<title>PHILIPPINES: Aboitiz gets fiscal perks for power plant.</title>
<headline>Aboitiz gets fiscal perks for power plant.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine Board of Investments said on Wednesday it approved the granting of fiscal incentives to Luzon Hydro Corp for the construction of a 3.15 billion peso, 70-megawatt hydro power plant in the northern Philippines.</p>
<p>Luzon Hydro is a joint venture between Aboitiz Equity Ventures, Transpac Hydro Inc and Filipino firms Ever Electrical Manufacturing Inc and Northern Mini Hydro Corp.</p>
<p>Transpac is owned by Transfield Holdings Overseas Pty Ltd of Australia and Pacific Hydro Ltd.</p>
<p>The firm was granted a six-year income tax holiday, a 3.0 percent duty on imported brand new capital equipment and tax credit on domestical capital equipment.</p>
<p>The power plant is scheduled to start operating on August 2001.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 fax 8176267</p>
</text>
